<p>
  This is the "about once a month" note from when you signed up.
</p>

<p>
  One thing worth doing if you will see your parent over Thanksgiving:
  spend ten minutes on what a phone call can't show you. Set their pill
  bottles out next to the medication list you have and look for three
  things: a bottle that isn't on the list, two bottles of the same
  medicine from different pharmacies or doctors, and old bottles that
  should have gone. If anything looks off, take a photo and ask their
  pharmacist, who will check it for free. While you're there, ring their
  phone from the room they sit in most and make sure they can hear it.
</p>

<%# Links are tagged ?from=monthly-note so a visit or sign-up from this note
    shows under its own name on Admin → Traffic. The setup-call offer links to
    its FAQ answer rather than to /setup-call: a click from an email arrives
    with no referrer, and the weekly report counts only setup-call clicks that
    came from our own pages (0.25.1), so a direct link would go uncounted. %>
<p>
  What has changed since last month: if your parent doesn't answer, Remindly
  can now ring you. For a reminder where being late matters, if none of the
  calls to your parent is answered, Remindly phones the family one at a time,
  in the order you choose, until someone presses 1 to say they'll check, and
  emails everyone else to say who's on it.
  <a href="<%= "#{ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST}/faq?from=monthly-note#if-they-still-dont-answer" %>">How it works</a>.
</p>

<p>
  And if you'd rather not set it up alone,
  <a href="<%= "#{ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST}/faq?from=monthly-note#setup-call" %>">book a free 15-minute call</a>
  and we'll do it with you on the phone: your parent, their first reminder,
  and what they'll hear.
</p>

<p>
  To start on your own, press "Set up reminders for my parent" on
  <a href="<%= "#{ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST}/?from=monthly-note" %>">the website</a>,
  and the link we email you creates your account.
</p>

<p>
  That is all — one note a month, nothing else.
  <a href="<%= "#{ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST}/subscribers/unsubscribe/#{@subscriber.signed_id(purpose: :unsubscribe)}" %>">Unsubscribe</a>
  any time, or just reply to this email to stop.
</p>

